From a07f89f469670d5e323947dde4409b019a14c3c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:32:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06911/11362] [outer-loop] dc22: D/8-twin lead closed, new
 bridge-latch route found (round 9)

Round-9 gpt-5.6-sol session used source inspection (development_proxy
provenance, not pure live-play) to definitively close the D/8-twin
question round 7-8 opened: only the LM checker ever receives the
color-cycle tag, quad clicks always advance by exactly one variant
regardless of order/timing, and the click path never branches on the
fail-timer value. No D/8 twin can be created by any click sequence.

Found the real mechanism instead: the wide 8-bar latch is polymorphic
-- driving the bare C-structure four positions left aligns it with a
separate, previously-untested 20x20 object (brixto-orckhi) instead of
the 8-ring, and the SAME latch click attaches that bridge. An offline
collision search found the bridge, once attached and carried via the
D-pad, connects R1 to the goal room.

A live attempt at this route failed on a wrong assumption (R1's C/B
checker isn't reachable directly from the R2 socket), not a wrong
mechanism -- the corrected path needs to route through LM first.
Independently re-verified by the outer loop: the full 517-action
attempt replays cleanly to level=5, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED,
matching the session's own report. No new level banked; frontier
stays at level 5. Flagged as the strongest lead this game has had
across 9 rounds -- next attempt should be a pure live execution of the
corrected route.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
